  "ingredients": [
    "2 medium fresh tomatoes",
    "1/4 cup olive oil",
    "salt and pepper (to taste)",
    "1/2 cup almond flour",
    "1 tablespoon psyllium husk powder",
    "2 tablespoon coconut flour",
    "1/4 teaspoon salt",
    "5 tablespoon butter (chilled)",
    "1/2 medium onion",
    "2 teaspoon fresh garlic",
    "2 tablespoon olive oil",
    "3 teaspoon fresh thyme",
    "3 ounce goat cheese"
  ],
  "instructions": [
    {
      "text": "Preheat oven to 425F. Slice the tomatoes into 1/4\" slices.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/goat-cheese-tomato-tarts/#wprm-recipe-51185-step-0-0",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/06/IMG_1596.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Lay the slices on a baking sheet lined with parchment paper. Drizzle over the olive oil and season with salt and pepper to taste. Use a toothpick to poke the tomatoes so that the juice can run out of the tomatoes and avoid steaming them.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/goat-cheese-tomato-tarts/#wprm-recipe-51185-step-0-1",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/06/IMG_1609.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Bake for 30–40 minutes or until roasted and most of the juice has evaporated.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/goat-cheese-tomato-tarts/#wprm-recipe-51185-step-0-2",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/06/IMG_1613.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Remove from the oven and set aside.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/goat-cheese-tomato-tarts/#wprm-recipe-51185-step-0-3",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/06/IMG_1618.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "In a food processor, combine the almond flour, psyllium husk, coconut flour, and salt.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/goat-cheese-tomato-tarts/#wprm-recipe-51185-step-0-4",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/06/IMG_1623.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cube the cold butter and add it into the food processor.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/goat-cheese-tomato-tarts/#wprm-recipe-51185-step-0-5",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/06/IMG_1626.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Slowly pulse the ingredients until a dough begins to form.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/goat-cheese-tomato-tarts/#wprm-recipe-51185-step-0-6",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/06/IMG_1627.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Press the dough into silicone cupcake molds, making the layers quite thin (about 1/4–1/2\").",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/goat-cheese-tomato-tarts/#wprm-recipe-51185-step-0-7",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/06/IMG_1639.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Reduce the oven temperature to 350F and bake the tarts for 17–20 minutes or until golden brown.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/goat-cheese-tomato-tarts/#wprm-recipe-51185-step-0-8",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/06/IMG_1645.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Remove from the oven and let cool. Once cooled, turn the silicone cupcake molds upside down and lightly tap the bottoms to slide the tarts out.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/goat-cheese-tomato-tarts/#wprm-recipe-51185-step-0-9",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/06/IMG_1650.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Layer the tomato slices over each tart.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/goat-cheese-tomato-tarts/#wprm-recipe-51185-step-0-10",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/06/IMG_1653.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Thinly slice the onion and mince the garlic. Heat up the olive oil in a pan and cook the onions and garlic until caramelized.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/goat-cheese-tomato-tarts/#wprm-recipe-51185-step-0-11",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/06/IMG_1661.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add the caramelized onions and garlic on top of the tomatoes.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/goat-cheese-tomato-tarts/#wprm-recipe-51185-step-0-12",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/06/IMG_1665.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Crumble the goat cheese and sprinkle fresh thyme over each tart. Bake for an additional 5–6 minutes or until the cheese is beginning to melt.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/goat-cheese-tomato-tarts/#wprm-recipe-51185-step-0-13",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/06/IMG_1677.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve warm!",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/goat-cheese-tomato-tarts/#wprm-recipe-51185-step-0-14",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/06/GoatCheeseTarts2.jpg"
    }
  ],
